# Title: Suspicious Scheduled Task Creation via Masqueraded XML File
# ID: dd2a821e-3b07-4d3b-a9ac-929fe4c6ca0c
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel, Elastic (idea)
# Date: 2023-04-20
# Tags: attack.privilege-escalation, attack.execution, attack.persistence, attack.stealth, attack.t1036.005, attack.t1053.005
# Description: Detects the creation of a scheduled task using the "-XML" flag with a file without the '.xml' extension. This behavior could be indicative of potential defense evasion attempt during persistence
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((((cmdline:*/create* OR cmdline:*-create*)) AND ((cmdline:*/xml* OR cmdline:*-xml*)) AND ((process_name:*\\schtasks.exe) OR (OriginalFileName:"schtasks.exe"))) AND -(((cmdline:*.xml*) OR (parent_name:*\\rundll32.exe AND (ParentCommandLine:*:\\WINDOWS\\Installer\\MSI* AND ParentCommandLine:*.tmp,zzzzInvokeManagedCustomActionOutOfProc*)) OR ((IntegrityLevel:"System" OR IntegrityLevel:"S-1-16-16384")))) AND -(((parent_name:*:\\ProgramData\\OEM\\UpgradeTool\\CareCenter_*\\BUnzip\\Setup_msi.exe OR parent_name:*:\\Program Files\\Axis Communications\\AXIS Camera Station\\SetupActions.exe OR parent_name:*:\\Program Files\\Axis Communications\\AXIS Device Manager\\AdmSetupActions.exe OR parent_name:*:\\Program Files (x86)\\Zemana\\AntiMalware\\AntiMalware.exe OR parent_name:*:\\Program Files\\Dell\\SupportAssist\\pcdrcui.exe))))
